ans:
If you need parameters or want to run multiple commands in sequence, use a shell function rather than an alias. Aliases don’t take parameters, so they’re only suitable for simple fixed text substitutions. For example, a function like:

pd() {
    pushd "$@"
    set_title_tab
}

lets you call `pd ~/Documents` and have the commands run in order. So the closest guidance is: use an alias for a simple shortcut with no arguments; use a shell function when the command needs arguments or more logic.

