You can build it by taking each adjacent pair of values and turning them into a linear segment over one unit of x.

For example, with data = {5, 1, 3, 8}, the segments are {5,1}, {1,3}, and {3,8}. A simple creator is:

createPiecewise[l_List] := Piecewise[MapIndexed[
  With[{pos = First[#2], y1 = First[#], y2 = Last[#]},
    {y1 (1 + pos - x) + y2 (x - pos), pos <= x < pos + 1}
  ] &,
  Partition[l, 2, 1]
]]

This uses Partition[l, 2, 1] to get adjacent pairs, then constructs a linear interpolation on each interval. You can then use Plot[createPiecewise[data], {x, 1, 4}] to visualize it.

If you want, I can also show how to adapt this for your example {1,1,1,0,0,1,1}.

