 Graphics[{Circle[], Rotate[Arrow[{{1, 0}, {1, 1}}], φ, {0, 0}]}],
 {φ, 0, 2 Pi}
]

You may also be interested in the two-argument form of ArcTan[x,y] (look it up in the docs).

ans:
If you only need a tangent to a circle, you can make a fixed arrow and rotate it as the point moves:

Manipulate[
 Graphics[{Circle[], Rotate[Arrow[{{1, 0}, {1, 1}}], φ, {0, 0}]}],
 {φ, 0, 2 Pi}
]

For an arbitrary curve, the closest guidance is to use the two-argument form ArcTan[x, y] rather than manually computing slopes, especially to handle vertical tangents correctly.

